00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:11.030
So an Ansible playbook is
a human-readable format

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.510
to holistically
describe an environment.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.880
In those playbooks, you have
tasks that are, by default,

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.180
executed sequentially in
order from top to bottom.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.370
And those tasks call
Ansible modules.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.280
And what modules are are the
tool kit in the language.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.270
They are what extends
Ansible and the simplicity

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:32.030
of the engine itself.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.840
So based on what
I'm reading here,

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.730
